  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -36pt;&quot;&gt;The applicant has failed to demonstrate that\r\nthe land is “agricultural land” as defined by Schedule 2, Part 6 D.1 of The\r\nTown and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015\r\nas amended. There is insufficient evidence to show that the land is in use as\r\nagricultural land and is so used for the purposes of a trade or business.\r\nFurthermore, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposal is\r\n“reasonably necessary” for the purpose of agriculture within the unit as\r\ndefined by Schedule 2, Part 6 Class A of The Town and Country Planning (General\r\nPermitted Development) (England) Order 2015 as amended.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -36pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
